  "notes": "{立|た}ち{上|あ}げる is a compound verb combining {立|た}つ (to stand) + {上|あ}げる (to raise), expressing the idea of getting something up and running.\n\nVERB TYPE:\n- Ichidan verb (る-verb)\n- Transitive\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {会社|かいしゃ}を{立|た}ち{上|あ}げる (to launch a company)\n- {事業|じぎょう}を{立|た}ち{上|あ}げる (to start a business)\n- プロジェクトを{立|た}ち{上|あ}げる (to launch a project)\n- パソコン/システムを{立|た}ち{上|あ}げる (to boot up a computer/system)\n- ウェブサイトを{立|た}ち{上|あ}げる (to launch a website)\n\nUSAGE:\n- Often used in business and IT contexts\n- The IT usage (boot up) comes from the physical metaphor of getting something standing and running\n- Compare with {起動|きどう}する which is more technical for systems\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {立|た}ち{上|あ}がる (intransitive: to stand up, to start up)\n- {起動|きどう}する (to start/boot - more technical)\n- {創業|そうぎょう}する (to found - more formal)\n\nREGISTER: Neutral. Common in business, IT, and everyday contexts.",
